cd "$(dirname "$0")"
P=..
./run2.sh liubei-ch2 new "Liu Bei (Xuande) of the Chinese Three Kingdoms era, about thirty-eight, the same man as in the first reference portrait but older: faint lines at the eyes and brow, a fuller moustache and goatee. He has just been named General of the Left by the Han court while living under Cao Cao's watch in Xuchang. FACE: calm, guarded and unreadable, a man who has learned to hide his heart; a quiet hardness under courtesy. POSE: his head is turned toward the RIGHT side of the picture and tilted slightly down, eyes lowered to the lower right as if quietly weighing something, body three-quarter view facing right (mirror of his earlier portraits, NOT looking left). COSTUME, clearly different from his earlier plain green scholar robe: a general's attire — dark iron lamellar shoulder guards and a breastplate edge visible over a deep olive-green war robe with dark trim, a broad leather belt with a bronze buckle, a short dark cloak, a black general's cap (not the scholar cap) with a small gold ornament; dignified, a new rank, not yet regal. One hand rests on the hilt of a sword at his waist. Background in light ink wash: the eaves of a capital palace and a distant gate tower under a pale overcast sky, faint." $P/liubei.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh liubei-ch3-ideal new "Liu Bei (Xuande) of the Chinese Three Kingdoms era, about forty-seven, the same man as in the first reference portrait but middle-aged: lines on the forehead and beside the nose, a long black beard and moustache with a trace of grey. COSTUME at the same level of richness as the second reference image (a ruler's fine attire): a deep green robe with gold-embroidered borders over an ivory inner robe, gilded steel shoulder pieces worn lightly, a black cap with a small gold crown ornament, a jade pendant at the sash; refined and noble, but softer and lighter than the second reference, not militaristic. FACE and POSE: he faces the viewer almost straight on, head level, chin neither raised nor lowered, looking directly and steadily into the viewer's eyes with calm, clear conviction; resolute, upright and graceful, warmth under strength; NOT looking down on the viewer, NOT domineering, NOT cold. Both hands rest together on the pommel of a sheathed sword planted before him. Background in light ink wash: spring mountains and terraced fields under clearing morning light, faint." $P/liubei.png liubei-ch3-yanyi.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh guanyu-ch2 edit "Edit the reference image. Keep the same man, face, angry expression, pose, glaive, beard, headscarf and rainy river background exactly. Change ONLY his clothing so that ARMOUR is more prominent: under the green robe show a visible dark iron lamellar cuirass on the chest and a large ornate gilded shoulder guard with a beast-head on the visible shoulder, and an iron bracer on the forearm gripping the glaive; the green robe is worn over the armour and partly opened to reveal it." guanyu-ch2-v1.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh guanyu-ch3 edit "Edit the reference image. Keep the same man, face, grey-streaked beard, arrogant expression, seated pose, bamboo book, glaive and flooded river background exactly. Change ONLY his clothing so that ARMOUR is prominent and magnificent, more than a robe: a full gilded and dark-green lacquered lamellar suit of armour on the chest and both shoulders, large gold beast-head pauldrons, a gold-trimmed armoured skirt over the knees, the green robe now only a mantle over the shoulders and sleeves; the armour of a famous senior general." guanyu-ch3-v1.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh zhangfei-ch3 edit "Edit the reference image. Keep EVERYTHING the same — the same man, face, beard, expression, armour, spear, pose and background — except: remove the coiled whip from his hand; instead his fist grips the hilt of a heavy sword at his belt. Also turn the wooden post in the background into a plain wooden army signal post with a hanging war drum (no noose, no gallows look)." zhangfei-ch3-v1.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh zhangfei-ch2 new "Zhang Fei (Yide) of the Chinese Three Kingdoms era, about thirty-four, the same man as in the first reference portrait (same broad swarthy face, round eyes, bristling tiger beard, black topknot with red band), slightly older, a small scar on one cheekbone. BODY: tall and powerful but with NATURAL proportions exactly like the first reference — normal shoulder width, NOT bulky oversized shoulders, NOT swollen armour. Composition is vertical in feel: standing tall and upright, the full height of his torso and the long serpent spear running from bottom to top of the frame. Inspired by his stand alone on the bridge at Changban: he plants the serpent spear upright beside him with one fist, the other fist on his hip, chest out, head raised, glaring down past the viewer as if challenging all under heaven to come at him; overwhelming dignity and force. MOUTH open in a commanding thunderous rebuke, as if shouting 'I am Zhang Yide of Yan! Who dares fight me to the death?', but controlled and majestic, not a wild scream, eyes fierce but steady. A green robe with dark iron shoulder guards (same size as the first reference), a red sash. Background in light ink wash: a narrow wooden bridge over a river with dust clouds and a dark wood beyond, faint." $P/zhangfei.png </dev/null &
sleep 2
./run2.sh caocao-B2-hegemon new "Cao Cao (Mengde) of the Chinese Three Kingdoms era, about forty-four, the same man as in the first reference portrait (same face, moustache and goatee) but older: lines on the brow and at the eyes, a fuller beard. The hegemon who holds the Emperor and crushes every rival by deceit and terror. POSE: he faces the viewer straight on (front view, NOT three-quarter), head tilted back and chin raised so that he looks DOWN at the viewer from above, eyelids half lowered in contempt, a cold arrogant, lawless look — he answers to no one; the viewpoint is slightly from below so he towers. A faint cruel tightening at one corner of the mouth (not a smile). COSTUME: black-lacquered steel armour over a deep blue robe, a blood-red cloak, a black cap with a gold ornament. Both hands rest on the pommel of a long sword planted point-down before him. Background in light ink wash: a burning walled city and crows in a smoke-darkened sky, faint." $P/caocao.png </dev/null &
wait
